H T 0~
frolicking bard~
the frolicking bard~
A drunken and loud bard frolicks across the stage, spouting wry tavern prose into the air.
~
   The bard is dressed in traditionally garish-colored livery worn by so many
of his trade.  A long, multicolored cape spins in the air with the bard's every
move.  His unruly mop of black hair surrounds a pale, fine featured face.  
Deep black eyes with smiling wrinkles rest utop a falcon-bridged nose, and fine
ruddy lips are constantly opened in one bawdy musical tale or another fancily
worded epic.  He strums a lyre in the air, drunkenly casting it about him but
always managing to play a perfect chord at the right instant.  Indeed, though
drunk he may be, his music only improves the warm and welcome atmosphere of
this restaurant.    
~
